--TEST--
A `var` key bound by a keyed `foreach` over a `Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>` has the map's key type, so `$tag->` offers `Tag`'s method and property, `rule:iteration/keyed-interfaces` and `rule:ide/completion-offers-only-what-the-compiler-derived`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Tag {
    public string $name = "red";
    public function label(): string { return $this->name; }
}
var $weights = new Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>();
foreach ($weights as var $tag => var $n) {
    echo $tag-><|>;
}
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
label() method    string
name    property  string
